## Why This Is Asked
This question explores a privacy-preserving on-device machine learning use case with real-world constraints including energy efficiency, latency requirements, data minimization principles, and regulatory compliance. It emphasizes the importance of measurable go/no-go criteria and a concrete break-even timeline for implementation decisions.

## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning models (autoencoder/isolation forest)
- Energy and performance budgeting for background tasks
- Data minimization and privacy impact assessments
- Go/No-Go criteria and break-even horizon analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function detectAnomaly(readings, threshold){
  const mean = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/readings.length;
  const variance = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+Math.pow(b-mean,2),0)/readings.length;
  return Math.abs(readings[readings.length-1] - mean) > threshold * Math.sqrt(variance);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to model costs for on-device features with privacy constraints, focusing on storage, compute, telemetry, and go/no-go criteria. It emphasizes practical trade-offs and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts
- On-device compute budgeting
- Data minimization and privacy compliance
- Telemetry design and cost optimization
- Index sizing and update cadence
- Break-even analysis and milestone-driven go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeCBA(params) {
  const storageCost = params.indexMB * 0.15;
  const energyCost = params.annualWh * 0.0003;
  const telemetryCost = params.dailyTelemetryKB * 365 * 0.00001;
  const privacyAuditCost = params.userCount * 0.10;

  return {
    storageCost,
    energyCost,
    telemetryCost,
    privacyAuditCost,
    totalYear1Cost: storageCost + energyCost + telemetryCost + privacyAuditCost
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cost-benefit framework for cross-app, on-device data sharing with strong privacy constraints and a realistic rollout plan.

## Key Concepts

- On-device cross-app data sharing with strict isolation
- User opt-out and privacy/compliance controls
- Resource budgeting: storage, CPU, energy
- Telemetry delta economics and governance
- Staged rollout and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: anonymize and bucket signals before local merge
function processEvent(event) {
  if (!userOptIn) return;
  const bucket = hash(event.type) % 10;
  buckets[bucket].push(event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and adapt to schema drift in shared signals?
- What rollback plan and telemetry safeguards would you implement if opt-out is toggled mid-rollout?

